course: dictionary
lesson: 6758
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The word open is a good example. Look at the words around it to find the meaning that fits. «The shop opens at nine o'clock» means the shop is ready for people to go in and use it.
explain: «An open oven door is hot enough to burn skin instantly.» Here open means not closed. The word door tells you what is open. Always ask: what does open mean in this sentence? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: «Keeping open food in tight boxes stops mice and insects from getting at it.» Here open means not covered. The context shows the meaning, so you do not need a dictionary. When one word has several meanings, the sentence around it decides which one you need.
fact: Open can be a verb, an adjective, or part of a phrase like «in the open».
fact: To open means to move something so you can go in or see inside, such as «open a box».
fact: Open means not closed. A shop or place is open when people can go in and use it.
fact: Open can also mean not covered or not fenced in, as in «the open sea».
fact: To open can mean to start, as in «The show opens on Friday».
exercise: «The shop opens at nine o'clock.» What does opens mean here? | The shop is covered with a roof | The shop is lifted up into the air | *The shop starts to be ready for people to go in and use it | The shop is closed for the day
exercise: «Keeping open food in tight boxes stops mice from getting at it.» What does open mean here? | Stuck shut tight | *Not covered | Very loud | Finished and gone
exercise: «The show opens on Friday.» Which word means the same as opens here? | Closes | *Starts | Moves inside | Covers
test: «She opened the box and found a gold key.» What does opened mean? | Closed it tight | Lost it in the grass | Painted it blue | *Moved the lid so she could look inside
test: In science, «an open circuit» has a gap, so no current flows. Why does no current flow? | It is too hot | It is full of water | It is covered in dust | *It has a gap in it
exam: Jayden says open always means the same thing. What is the best answer? | No, open only means to start a show | Yes, open always means not covered | Yes, open always means not closed | *No, open has several meanings, so check the words around it
